## Context

Split off from 1244 (child 1 of tracker 1226), criterion 3, by the author's
ruling of 2026-10-27. 1244's runner, on red, prints the would-be ticket text
(tip, failing checks, first-parent merges since the last green after-record)
and exits non-zero; it writes nothing to the forge. This ticket makes that red
reach a ticket without a human.

## Finding that forced the split

The raid feasibility check of 1244 found that the bookkeeping tier in
`.merge-gate.json` (`"tiers": {"bookkeeping": [...]}`) still runs
`pytest-guard` on the candidate (main tip plus the ticket file). When the
after-merge red is `pytest-guard`, the likely case, a ticket-only PR fails its
own before-merge record and can never merge on the bookkeeping path: the
autoland deadlocks exactly when it fires. Check: plant a failing test on a
temp main and run `merge-gate.py run` on a ticket-only candidate.

Remedies to weigh: file the red outside a merge (a forge issue behind an
extension point, the ticket then landing with the fix), or a bookkeeping
check set that does not run the suite for a red-ticket candidate.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A red after-merge record opens a ticket naming the tip, the failing checks and the merges since the last green tip; a test shows it on a planted failure, and a second red run on the same failure opens no second ticket.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/merge-gate.py` (`run-after`, `red_report`)
- `.merge-gate.json` (`tiers`)
- `skills/merge/SKILL.md` step 9

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27, wave 4)
- GO once 1245 lands: a ticket-only PR's before-merge record then runs the cheap set, not pytest-guard.
- Path: `open_red_ticket(report, tip)` in scripts/merge-gate.py, called from `run_after` on FAIL; writes
  `tickets/<next>-after-merge-red-<tip12>.erg` from `red_report` in a throwaway worktree on branch
  `red-<tip12>`, commits, pushes, records the before-merge gate, lands by the /merge flow; serialized
  under the runner's existing lock, bounded retries.
- Dedupe key: the sorted failing-check set (not the tip, which moves on every merge of a red main);
  skip when an open ticket or a remote `red-*` branch carries the same set.
- First test: temp main with a failing check, `run-after` twice: one ticket after the first run, still
  one after the second; the file passes `tickets/erg check`.
- Overlap: 1254 also edits `red_report` (match failing checks by name); land one at a time.
